{"The default value `timezone.now()` is evaluated at class definition time, not at instance creation time, causing all instances without explicit `queued` value to share the same timestamp - should use `field(default_factory=timezone.now)` instead": 0.924540638923645, "Silently returning `None` on deserialization failure in `from_dict()` creates an observability gap and can disable loop protection when payloads are malformed or schema drift occurs - should add logging or metrics": 0.8391894102096558, "When `assignment_source_dict` is provided but deserialization fails (returns `None`), the sync proceeds as if no source was provided, potentially re-enabling sync loops - should add logging or metrics to track when this happens": 0.7942745089530945, "Loop prevention scope is narrow - only blocks immediate echo-back to the originating integration, leaving exposure to multi-hop cycles (A \u2192 Sentry \u2192 B \u2192 Sentry \u2192 A) and concurrent update scenarios unaddressed": 0.5652263164520264, "Missing validation on `integration_id` and `source_name` fields means edge cases and misconfigurations could slip through": 0.676148533821106}